{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Mirror inventory finding F8 (`reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md`), LOW.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe relation vocabulary has three sides that agree today:\n\n- `src/rebar/types.py:24` `Relation` and `schemas/common.schema.json#/$defs/relation` — canonical\n- `src/rebar/graph/_links.py:20` `CANONICAL_RELATIONS` — the same 7, hand-copied, and the gate for\n  link creation at `:173`\n\n`tests/interfaces/contracts/test_event_schema_relations.py:23` already pins `CANONICAL_RELATIONS`\nto `docs/event-schema.md`. So the DOC arm is gated and the SCHEMA arm is not: a relation could be\nadded to the schema and the docs while `CANONICAL_RELATIONS` rejected it at `:173`, or removed from\nthe schema while the code still accepted it, with the existing test green either way.\n\nThis is preventive — all three currently hold the same 7 values, verified.\n\n## Approach — add-parity-check\n\nExtend the existing contract test with the missing arm: `CANONICAL_RELATIONS` equals\n`set(get_args(Relation))` equals the schema's `$defs.relation.enum`. One test, three-way, so no\npair can drift while another agrees.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1: the test asserts all three sides are equal, reading the real objects and the real schema\n      file rather than re-listing the relations. Verified by it passing on the committed tree.\n- [ ] AC2: the assertion fails when ANY one side diverges, naming which. Verified by three mutation\n      checks, one per side, each RED with the offending relation in the message.\n- [ ] AC3: the existing docs arm still passes unchanged. Verified by the original test remaining\n      green and untouched in behavior.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `python -m pytest tests/interfaces/contracts/test_event_schema_relations.py -q` — AC1-AC3.\n- `make lint && make typecheck`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788385002586489001,"uuid":"4be133d4-180d-40af-b5c9-ef72b000a646"}